(7718884, 1269603, 100831, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> I was actually thinking of this photo, which turns out was Robert Freeman, not Astrid:<br/> <br/><a href="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2019/11/13/obituaries/11Freeman-sub/11Freeman-sub-superJumbo.jpg?quality=75&amp;auto=webp" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">https://static01.nyt.com/images/2019/11/13/obituaries/11Freeman-sub/11Freeman-sub-superJumbo.jpg?quality=75&amp;auto=webp</a> <br/> <br/>I had read somewhere that Astrid did side lighting like that, but I could be misremembering. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks.  Maybe you meant this.   <a href="//www.silverkgallery.com.au/astrid/astrid.htm" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Astrid</a>.      <br/> <br/>But either way, Im flattered.</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: I was actually thinking of this photo, which turns out was Robert Freeman, not Astrid: https://static01.nyt.com/images/2019/11/13/obituaries/11Freeman-sub/11Freeman-sub-superJumbo.jpg?quality=75&auto=webp  I had read somewhere that Astrid did side lighting like that, but I could be misremembering.   Thanks.  Maybe you meant this.   Astrid.       But either way, Im flattered.', '2022-04-19 00:00:32.000000', NULL, 0),
